<reference id="_Toc238560390" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 8: Table with an empty cell</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a Markdown table that shows operating system support for different deployment features. Some features</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Supported</keyword>
        <keyword>empty</keyword>
        <keyword>Windows</keyword>
        <keyword>Integration</keyword>
        <keyword>Table</keyword>
        <keyword>table</keyword>
        <indexterm>Supported</indexterm>
        <indexterm>empty</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Windows</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section><p>Consider a Markdown table that shows operating system support for different deployment features. Some features may not be available on every platform, resulting in intentionally empty cells.</p>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Table with an empty cell</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>.md input </entry>
                     <entry>DITA output </entry>
                  </row>                  
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <pre>| Feature | Windows | Linux | macOS |
  |----------|----------|----------|----------|
  | Email Notifications | Supported | Supported | Supported |
  | Windows Event Log Integration | Supported | | |
  | Systemd Service Integration | | Supported | |</pre>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <pre>
                           
                              
                                 Feature
                                 Windows
                                 Linux
                                 macOS
                              
                              
                                 Email Notifications
                                 Supported
                                 Supported
                                 Supported
                              
                              
                                 Windows Event Log Integration
                                 Supported
                                 
                                 
                              
                              
                                 Systemd Service Integration
                                 
                                 Supported
                                 
                              
                           
                        </pre>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p>
   <b>Result:</b>Empty Markdown table cells are converted into empty DITA <codeph>&lt;stentry/&gt;</codeph>
         elements. The converter preserves the table structure and column alignment even when some
         values are missing.</p></section></refbody>
</reference>
